  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Contact Sheet",
    "overview": "Triage is editing a roll of film. Every article in the list is a numbered frame printed beside a solid rebate band; the frames you have not looked at print bright, the ones you have fade, keepers are ringed with a china marker, and the article you open is the enlargement. The board the sheet lies on is cool grey, the print itself is photo-paper white, and nothing else in the chrome asks for attention. Density is a working editor's density: tight rows, a 2rem toolbar at the desk, 44px targets under a thumb.\n\nThe two themes are co-equal and are one material read two ways. The light theme is **the print**: white paper, black rebate, deep marker. The dark theme is **the negative**: graphite paper, a light rebate, and a brighter marker. Every component references roles only (`--surface-*`, `--text-*`, `--border-*`, `--ink-select`, `--rebate*`, `--accent`), so a component written once is correct in both.\n\nColour carries exactly two jobs. Ink (`--ink-select`) is selection: whatever is chosen right now is inverted. The marker (`--accent`) is judgement: keepers, links and focus, nothing else. The marker is the user's own pen, one of seven colours, red by default. The system rejects the grey-sidebar, blue-accent three-pane reader with dot-only unread state that this world replaced.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A solid rebate band down the article list's left edge, carrying two-digit mono frame numbers that scroll with the rows.",
      "Selection is ink (black on the print, near-white on the negative), never the marker.",
      "The marker colour (`--accent`) appears only for keeper state, links and keyboard focus.",
      "Hanken Grotesk for the interface, Literata for reading, JetBrains Mono for numbers only.",
      "Corners are cut square and only softened (3px); the one curve is the hand-drawn keeper ring.",
      "Flat surfaces stepped by tone; shadows exist only on things that float above the sheet."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink Selects, The Marker Judges Rule",
        "body": "Selection (the active feed, the checked segment, the highlighted palette row, the toggled toolbar button) is always `ink-select` with `on-ink-select`. The marker is never used to show selection, and ink is never used to show a keeper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Marker's Three Jobs Rule",
        "body": "`--accent` paints exactly three things: keeper state, links, and keyboard focus. If a new element wants the marker and is none of those, it doesn't get it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Roles Only Rule",
        "body": "Components reference role tokens, never raw hex values. The marker derivations (`--accent-hover`, `--focus-ring`) are declared on `body`, not `:root`, so they resolve against the selected `data-accent`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numbers Are Mono Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono sets numbers that line up (frame numbers, frame tags, counts) and code, and nothing else. Words are never set in mono outside code and the user's own mono reading choice.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight Is Unread Rule",
        "body": "Unread is shown by weight (600 against 400) and a brighter frame number, and this signal survives grayscale. Opacity is never used to show that something has been read.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Sheet Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces on the sheet (rows, cards, panes, the reader) carry no drop shadow. Only overlays (the palette, toasts, menus) lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Square Print Rule",
        "body": "Corners soften but never round. Anything that reads as a print, a frame or a control stays at 3px or less; only the hand-drawn marker ring and the swatches curve.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** show selection in ink (`--ink-select` / `--on-ink-select`) in both themes.",
      "**Do** reserve `--accent` for keeper state, links and keyboard focus, and use `--marker-on-rebate` for any marker drawn on the rebate band.",
      "**Do** number frames with two-digit tabular mono (`01`, `02`…) and show unread state with weight and brightness, never with colour alone.",
      "**Do** design every new component against the print and the negative together, using role tokens only.",
      "**Do** keep corners at 3px (2px for stamps) and keep the sheet flat; lift only overlays.",
      "**Do** keep meta, placeholders and captions at `--text-tertiary` or stronger, never lowered with opacity.",
      "**Do** give touch controls a 44px minimum and confine hover feedback to `(hover: hover)`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use the marker for selection, active tabs or toggled controls; selection is ink.",
      "**Don't** fill or flood the selected frame; outline it in ink.",
      "**Don't** set words in JetBrains Mono outside code and the user's mono reading choice.",
      "**Don't** round prints, cards or controls past 3px.",
      "**Don't** add drop shadows to rows, cards or panes on the sheet.",
      "**Don't** show unread with only a coloured dot; weight is the signal.",
      "**Don't** hard-code a colour in a component when a role token exists."
    ]
